    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="section" id="takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Never evaluate on training data</strong> — it creates an illusion of performance due to overfitting and data memorization</li>
        <li><strong>Use three-way splits:</strong> Train for learning, validation for tuning and early stopping, test for final unbiased evaluation</li>
        <li><strong>Stratify when necessary</strong> — for imbalanced classification, ensure representative class distributions across splits</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-validation for small datasets</strong> — k-fold CV maximizes data usage and provides robust performance estimates with confidence intervals</li>
        <li><strong>Protect the test set</strong> — never use it during development; evaluate it only once at the very end</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

